{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make test_overview_summaries_free_of_removed_constructs assert each AFFECTED command is present in the overview (or drive it from the parsed overview keys) instead of silently `continue`-ing on a lookup miss.","criteria":["error-handling","tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py:142: `line = lines.get(sub)`","tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py:143: `if line is None:`","tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py:144: `continue`","The line key is derived from `line.split()[0]` (line 137), so any change to overview formatting or a dropped command makes the lookup miss and the assertions on lines 145-147 never execute — 'the check produces its verdict' and 'the command was never checked' are indistinguishable."],"finding":"In test_overview_summaries_free_of_removed_constructs, a command whose overview one-liner is not found (`lines.get(sub)` returns None) is silently skipped via `if line is None: continue`, so a missing/renamed overview entry passes the test identically to a checked-clean one — the em-dash/en-dash/semicolon guard never runs for that command.","id":"0","impact":0.225,"location":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py:141","norm_id":"n144766c381b211f9","priority":0.1928,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A future refactor renames or removes a command's overview entry, or reflows the overview so the first token differs, and the em-dash/semicolon regression for that command goes uncaught."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Replace the `if line is None: continue` skip with an explicit `assert line is not None, f\"overview missing {sub}\"` so a missing overview entry fails loudly rather than passing vacuously.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Anchor test_overview_summaries_free_of_removed_constructs with a liveness check that the affected commands were actually found in the overview before trusting the absence assertions.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py:142-144: `line = lines.get(sub)` then `if line is None: continue`","The dict is keyed by `line.split()[0]` for lines starting with two spaces (lines 136-140); a format change or a missing command yields None and the assertions on lines 145-147 never run","No assertion anchors producer liveness (e.g. that any/all AFFECTED commands were found in `lines`) before trusting the em-dash/semicolon absence checks — the check produces its passing verdict both when summaries are clean AND when nothing matched"],"finding":"test_overview_summaries_free_of_removed_constructs silently skips (continue) any affected command not found in the parsed overview lines, with no assertion that at least the affected commands were located; the test passes vacuously if overview parsing matches nothing or an affected command drops out of the overview, so it cannot distinguish 'all summaries clean' from 'the producer emitted nothing matchable'.","id":"1","impact":0.225,"location":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py:141","norm_id":"n589c0239f745ec56","priority":0.1928,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":["An affected command's overview one-liner is dropped or its leading whitespace/format changes so `line.split()[0]` no longer keys it — the removed-construct assertions are silently skipped and the test still passes","A future regression reintroduces an em dash but simultaneously changes the overview line shape so the command key no longer matches"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Replace the silent `continue` with a presence assertion, e.g. `assert line is not None, f\"overview missing summary for {sub}\"`, or assert `set(AFFECTED) <= lines.keys()` before the loop so a vanished/unmatched command fails the test instead of passing vacuously.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_miti